{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>For this commandment.</b> And the reason I said, וַהֲשֵׁבֹתָ אֶל לְבָבֶךָ בְּכָל הַגּוֹיִם — that your repentance must take place while you are yet in exile, in order that you may be saved — is that truly this commandment of repentance which I command you today, as stated with regard to every sin in the section of Leviticus (Leviticus 5:5), וְאָשֵׁם וְאָשְׁמוּ, whose meaning in all cases is that the sinner acknowledge his sin, as he explained afterward in saying, וְהָיָה כִי יֶאְשַׁם לְאַחַת מֵאֵלֶּה וְהִתְוַדָּה אֲשֶׁר חָטָא עָלֶיהָ, and likewise in saying (Numbers 5:6–7), אִישׁ אוֹ אִשָּׁה כִּי יַעֲשׂוּ מִכָּל חַטֹּאת הָאָדָם וְאָשְׁמָה הַנֶּפֶשׁ הַהִוא וְהִתְוַדּוּ אֶת עֲוֹנָם.</p>" "<b>It is not beyond you.</b> That you would require prophets." "<b>It is not distant.</b> That you would require the sages of a distant generation to explain it to you so that you are able to do it, even while you are yet in exile. And he explained this in saying:"], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:22:41.628631160Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}